{{also|runoff|run off with|run-off}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-run off.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|run<,,ran,run> off}}

# To [[flee]] or [[depart]] quickly.
#: {{ux|en|Don't '''run off''' before the end of the event.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''ran off''' to France leaving her with all the debts and three children to bring up.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1966|author={{w|The Kinks}}|title=Sunny Afternoon
|passage=My girlfriend's '''run off''' with my car<br>And gone back to her ma and pa.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To make [[photocopies]], or [[print]].
#: {{ux|en|Please '''run off''' a couple dozen more flyers to pass out.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[write]] something quickly.
#: {{ux|en|Shakespeare could '''run off''' a play in just a couple of days.}}
# (of a [[liquid]]) To [[pour]] or [[spill]] [[off]] or [[over]].
#: {{ux|en|They kept a barrel to store rainwater that has '''run off''' the roof.}}
# To cause to flow away.
#: {{ux|en|to '''run off''' a charge of molten metal from a furnace}}
# To [[chase]] someone away.
#: {{ux|en|If anyone comes into this field, the bull will soon '''run''' them '''off'''.}}
# To [[operate]] by a particular [[energy]] or [[fuel]] source.
#: {{ux|en|This radio '''runs off''' batteries.}}
# To have [[diarrhea]].

